in today's video i'll give you 10 games  to play while you're waiting for  hogwarts legacy  retrorecontour here i'm just a dad who  loves games and the stories they tell  and like so many of you  i'm eagerly awaiting the release of  hogwarts legacy but there are so  many video games released these days  there are plenty we can play in the  meantime to fill that void until  hogwarts legacy finally arrives sometime  in 2022  each of these titles contains at least  some element i feel would appeal to fans  of harry potter and those looking  forward to hogwarts legacy  some have really good stories whereas  others are action rpgs like  hogwarts legacy some on the list are  fairly recent and  others are pretty old if you decide you  want to pick up any of these titles i'll  have links down in the description box  below  number one the old harry potter games  okay we might as well start with the  obvious ones right because if you  haven't played any of the old harry  potter games there are actually quite a  few worth playing even if they aren't  out of this world great games i've  played quite a few of them over the  years in fact i'm actually doing a let's  play  right now here on the channel if you're  curious you can check that out as well  the easiest ones to get your hands on  these days are the lego harry potter  games which are available on  all the major consoles as well as pc as  for the older console on pc games and  unfortunately they're a little difficult  to find but google and reddit can help  you there  you can always look to buy secondhand  physical copies through a local game  shop or ebay  i recently purchased a ps3 copy of order  of the phoenix on ebay for around 15  bucks  you can probably find them pretty cheap  my personal favorites are the original  sorcerer stone game on pc  the console version of chamber of  secrets and the previously mentioned  order of the phoenix  all the lego games are pretty good as  well but once you've played one of those  lego games you kind of know what you're  getting into with all  a lot of folks are partial to the wii  version of order of the phoenix but if  the novelty of motion controls has worn  off for you  if it has for me you can stick to one of  the other versions instead  sadly i think most fans feel as if we  are still waiting for a truly  great harry potter game while a lot of  these games are enjoyable in their own  way i personally don't feel that any of  them truly lived up to the potential of  what a harry potter game can be  so no pressure hogwarts legacy the  history of the royal  family of hyrule is also the history of  the calamity ganon number two the legend  of zelda breath of the wild  if you have a nintendo switch then  chances are you're already one of the 22  million who have purchased the game  but if you haven't played it yet you  should change that as soon as  possible heck even if you've already  played it's worth playing again or going  back to your original save to try and  complete more quests  overall the zelda series probably has  more in common with fantasy titles like  lure the rings  but harry potter fans will no doubt  enjoy the vast exploration and freedom  you have with such an open game like  breath of the wild  of course there are magic items and  abilities link obtains throughout his  journey as well  where the game really shines is in the  freedom it gives you to solve  problems and complete challenges using  the magic and abilities at your disposal  even years after its release people were  still finding different ways to  accomplish tasks throughout the game  [Music]  number three persona 4 golden persona 4  is the first persona game i played and  yes i played  the ps vita version long live the vida  persona 4 is a japanese rpg developed by  atlas and you'll play as a high school  student who starts investigating a  series of mysterious murders  the appeal here for harry potter fans is  in the relationships and drama between  high school teenagers persona 4 has a  unique social link system where  developing your friendships will yield  bonuses and enhancements during battle  the kicker is like the real world  there's only so much time in the day so  you can't spend time with every single  friend  you'll have to choose who you spend your  time with admittedly the game  is long but the story is riveting it's  characters fun and interesting and the  persona battle system is one i really  enjoy  at number four we have ori and the blind  forest this one completely shifting  gears from something like persona  ori on the other hand is a  side-scrolling platformer that also has  elements of something like metroid or  castlevania you'll unlock an upgrade  abilities along your journey through the  game with absolutely  gorgeous graphics the art here is just  staggering  all of these elements combine to help  tell what is a touching story that i  really think will resonate with harry  potter fans  [Applause]  at number five we have the witcher 3  wild hunt  look you knew it had to be on the list  fantasy game  in the action rpg genre hogwarts legacy  fans if you haven't played this one yet  you gotta give it a shot it's based on a  series of polish novels so it's no  surprise that the video game version is  rich with a deep backstory  interesting characters and a well  thought out magic system  personally i'm not a huge fan of the  combat and how it controls overall but  everything else is an absolute 10 out of  10 for me  seriously this would probably be my  favorite game ever made if it had the  combat of something like dark souls  the level of detail throughout the world  is just staggering you'll have  choices and dialogue options throughout  that let you control how you want to  handle certain confrontations  wild hunt also has some of the best side  quests in  any game i've played there are side  quests here with completely dynamic  characters and overall the side quests  feel  even more fleshed out than something you  would see in an entire game  if you're a fan of good stories epic  fantasy and using magic then you owe it  to yourself to give the witcher 3 a try  number six we're gonna completely shift  gears yet again  and say animal crossing new horizons  look i admit this may seem like an odd  recommendation for harry potter fans  it's not an action rpg you don't really  use  magic so what's the appeal here i've  personally found there to be some  overlap between  harry potter and animal crossing fans  for those of you very familiar with my  channel here you know i have quite a few  animal crossing videos in addition to  the harry potter ones  so what is it about animal crossing that  appeals to so many harry potter fans for  me i think a lot of it is about the  creativity you have in animal crossing  you can design areas that look like  hogwarts castle decorate your house to  look like the common room of your choice  and of course you can dress like a  wizard as well  you can also design clothing to  represent your favorite house or  quidditch team  and look we all know the harry potter  series provided a great escape from the  real world for so many of us and animal  crossing really does the same  it's a calming slower paced game that's  more about the overall experience than  trying to complete objective after  objective  in their tongue dragonborn  number seven the elder scrolls 5 skyrim  skyrim was the first elder scrolls game  i ever played and it completely  blew me away from the first moment i had  control of my character  i went straight for the college of  winterhold where i had heard you could  learn  magic what awaited me there was a series  of stories and missions that could have  been an entire game  on their own the world felt alive and i  truly felt a bond forming between my  player and the other characters at the  college  there's plenty of magic for harry potter  fans and an expansive lore about the  world and creatures to go along with it  it's true skyrim is one of the older  titles on the list but if you have yet  to play  i highly recommend it ashton won  here is thou my voice still  number eight dark souls three if you're  looking for something that's a little  more challenging than what we've had so  far on the list  look no further than the soul series i  went with dark souls 3 for the list here  even though  one is probably my favorite overall but  you can't go wrong with either of them  definitely would not recommend starting  with two though dark souls 3 has some of  the  best bosses in the entire series and yes  there's plenty  of magic bloodborne and demon souls are  also fantastic  honestly bloodborne is probably my  favorite souls game overall but since  this is a list  specifically for harry potter fans i  went with a souls game here because they  do  have more magic overall than what you  would see in something like bloodborne  and if you can get your hands on a ps5  then the demon souls remaster is  absolutely fantastic  find your way home number nine god of  war  the 2018 version of god of war  completely reinvented the series in  all the right ways pulling elements from  both greek and norse mythology there's  both magic  and creatures that will certainly please  harry potter fans  as good as the action is in the new god  of war though the series also  incorporated more upgradability and  freedom in the abilities you unlock  but the heart of the game is absolutely  the relationship between kratos and his  son atreus  harry longed for a father figure  throughout the entire harry potter  series and frequently sought the  approval of the prominent male  influences in his life  such as dumbledore lupin and of course  sirius  seeing kratos and atreus bond throughout  the adventure and playing out their  journey with some  epic moments of action is one of the  most impactful moments i've had in  gaming  over the past decade  number 10 star wars knights of the old  republic  and here we have one of my favorite  action rpgs of all time  there's actually been some chatter that  hogwarts legacy will have elements  inspired by knights of the old republic  and let me tell you i'd certainly love  it if that were the case  this is another older one on our list  but still definitely worth playing i  would say there's one key element here  that this one has over any of the others  on our list  and that's the sense of choice yes  choice is present in some of the other  games but here  it really stands out through various  dialogue choices and a somewhat  branching story knights of the old  republic gave players the ability to  become a good jedi  or an evil sith there were also unique  abilities based on your path of choice  and for anyone who's already played it  you guys already know the epic twist at  the end  rivals that it was plural moment that we  had in sorcerer's stone  these days you can usually find this one  and its sequel for pretty cheap over on  steam  and you know what i'm going to throw in  one bonus option for the multiplayer  fans out there and that would be  spell break instead of guns with spell  break this is a title focused on  spell casting to take down your  opponents you can choose to wield fire  as a pyromancer  shift the earth as a stone shaper poison  foes as the toxicologist  electrify enemies as a conduit freeze  foes as a frostborn or do your best  airbender impersonation as the tempest  class  this one is actually free to play as  well and it's available on all major  platforms so if it sounds like something  you'd be interested in there's no reason  not to try  which of the games on this list are your  favorite and do you have any other  recommendations for your fellow harry  potter fans out there  i want to hear it in the comments below  so let me know and as always guys thank  you all so much for watching  i'll talk to you again soon

